{
  "messages": [
    {
      "time": "14:15",
      "author": "Timo Laine",
      "role": "Field Engineer",
      "text": "Hi Pirjo, I just changed the SFP on TRN-033 at site OULU-03. The link is up and optics look normal, but the counters are at zero and there is no traffic passing through."
    },
    {
      "time": "14:18",
      "author": "Pirjo Heikkinen",
      "role": "Network Expert",
      "text": "Hi Timo. That is weird if the optical levels are fine. Did you try a hard shut/no shut on the port?"
    },
    {
      "time": "14:20",
      "author": "Timo Laine",
      "role": "Field Engineer",
      "text": "Yes, tried that and also bounced the interface, but still same. Link is green but zero packets moving."
    },
    {
      "time": "14:23",
      "author": "Pirjo Heikkinen",
      "role": "Network Expert",
      "text": "I think it might be the SFP batch, maybe try another vendor. I am not 100% sure though, I have not seen this behavior myself before."
    },
    {
      "time": "14:26",
      "author": "Timo Laine",
      "role": "Field Engineer",
      "text": "Ok, I don't have other brands with me today. I will look for another vendor's SFP tomorrow from the warehouse and try that. Thanks!"
    }
  ]
}
